.Dd @NCOLLECTD_DATE@
.Dt NCOLLECTD-ROUTEROS 5
.Os ncollectd @NCOLLECTD_VERSION@
.Sh NAME
.Nm ncollectd-routeros
.Nd Documentation of ncollectd's routeros plugin
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Bd -literal -compact
\fBload-plugin\fP routeros
\fBplugin\fP routeros {
    \fBinstance\fP \fIname\fP {
        \fBhost\fP \fIhost\fP
        \fBport\fP \fIport\fP
        \fBssl\fP \fItrue|false\fP
        \fBca-cert\fP \fI/path/to/ca\fP
        \fBverify-peer\fP \fItrue|false\fP
        \fBverify-host\fP \fItrue|false\fP
        \fBuser\fP \fIuser\fP
        \fBuser-env\fP \fIenv-name\fP
        \fBpassword\fP \fIpassword\fP
        \fBpassword-env\fP \fIenv-name\fP
        \fBtimeout\fP \fIseconds\fP
        \fBinterval\fP \fIseconds\fP
        \fBfilter\fP {
            ...
        }
    }
}
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The \fBrouteros\fP plugin connects to a device running \fIRouterOS\fP, the
Linux-based operating system for routers by \fIMikroTik\fP.
The configuration supports querying multiple routers:
.Pp
The \fBrouteros\fP plugin consists of one or more \fBinstance\fP blocks.
Within each block, the following options are understood:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \fBhost\fP \fIhost\fP
Hostname or IP-address of the router to connect to.
.It \fBport\fP \fIport\fP
Port name or port number used when connecting.
If left unspecified, "8728" is used, or "8729" (the \fIapi-ssl\fP service)
when \fBssl\fP is enabled.
.It \fBssl\fP \fItrue|false\fP
Connect to the \fIapi-ssl\fP service of the router using TLS.
Without TLS the user name, the password and all the data are sent in
clear text over the network.
The router must have a certificate assigned to the \fIapi-ssl\fP service:
without one RouterOS only offers anonymous ciphers, which are not accepted.
Defaults to \fIfalse\fP.
.It \fBca-cert\fP \fI/path/to/ca\fP
File with the PEM-encoded CA certificates used to verify the certificate
of the router.
If not set, the default CA certificates of the system are used.
.It \fBverify-peer\fP \fItrue|false\fP
Enable or disable the verification of the certificate of the router.
Enabled by default.
.It \fBverify-host\fP \fItrue|false\fP
Enable or disable the check that the certificate of the router matches
the host name or address given in \fBhost\fP.
Only used when \fBverify-peer\fP is enabled.
Enabled by default.
.It \fBuser\fP \fIuser\fP
Use the user name \fIuser\fP to authenticate.
Defaults to "admin".
It is recommended to use a dedicated user with read-only rights
(a group with the policies \fIread\fP and \fIapi\fP) instead.
.It \fBuser-env\fP \fIenv-name\fP
Get the user name \fIuser\fP to authenticate from the environment
variable \fIenv-name\fP.
.It \fBpassword\fP \fIpassword\fP
Set the password used to authenticate.
.It \fBpassword-env\fP \fIenv-name\fP
Get the password used to authenticate from the environment
variable \fIenv-name\fP.
.It \fBtimeout\fP \fIseconds\fP
Timeout for establishing the connection to the router and for every
read or write on it, rounded to whole seconds (at least one second).
If the router does not respond in time the connection is closed and
reopened in the next interval.
Defaults to half of the \fBinterval\fP.
.It \fBinterval\fP \fIseconds\fP
Sets the interval (in seconds) in which the values will be collected
from this instance.
By default the global \fBinterval\fP setting will be used.
.It \fBfilter\fP
Configure a filter to modify or drop the metrics.
See \fBFILTER CONFIGURATION\fP in
.Xr ncollectd.conf 5 .
.El
.Sh "SEE ALSO"
.Xr ncollectd 1 ,
.Xr ncollectd.conf 5
